$ floe part check
exit 1
--- stderr
$SAMPLE/own/parts/Note: floe takes no such name: write lower case letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter or a digit; rename it
$SAMPLE/own/parts/base: base names a file of every theme (base.css), which a theme's CSS for this part would be read as: give it another name
$SAMPLE/own/parts/table: table is the name of floe's parts/table, which floe's templates and parts would go on drawing and checking with: give yours another name
$ floe check page.yaml
exit 1
--- stderr
$SAMPLE/own/parts/Note: floe takes no such name: write lower case letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter or a digit; rename it
$SAMPLE/own/parts/base: base names a file of every theme (base.css), which a theme's CSS for this part would be read as: give it another name
$SAMPLE/own/parts/table: table is the name of floe's parts/table, which floe's templates and parts would go on drawing and checking with: give yours another name
$ floe render --out-dir $TMP/pages/page.yaml page.yaml
exit 1
--- stderr
$SAMPLE/own/parts/Note: floe takes no such name: write lower case letters, digits, - and _, starting with a letter or a digit; rename it
$SAMPLE/own/parts/base: base names a file of every theme (base.css), which a theme's CSS for this part would be read as: give it another name
$SAMPLE/own/parts/table: table is the name of floe's parts/table, which floe's templates and parts would go on drawing and checking with: give yours another name
